# Util stack secrets (services VM) — ExcaliDash only
# Copy to .sops.env and encrypt with:
#   SOPS_AGE_KEY_FILE=../../sops_age_key.txt sops -e -i .sops.env
#
# Key-set contract: this file, the real .sops.env and the test fixture
# tests/fixtures/util.sops.env must all carry EXACTLY the same keys — the
# stack-env-drift lint fails on any difference.
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE'S EXISTENCE CHANGES HOW THE WHOLE STACK SYNCS. Before it,
# stacks/util had no env_file at all, so bentopdf and mazanoke synced with
# nothing to validate. Only excalidash-backend declares env_file, and it uses
# the LONG FORM (`path: .env, required: false`) — the plain form fails Arcane's
# staged sync validation, where the host-decrypted .env cannot exist yet, and
# that failure aborts the sync of the ENTIRE stack (finding #11). Getting that
# wrong would take bentopdf and mazanoke down with it.
#
# Reminder from CLAUDE.md, and verified empirically (finding #30): Compose
# INTERPOLATES env_file values, so any value containing '$' must be
# single-quoted in the plaintext before encrypting. None of the generate
# commands below emit '$'.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ExcaliDash session and CSRF secrets.
#
# ⚠ SET THEM EXPLICITLY. Upstream auto-generates both and PERSISTS them into
# the data volume if they are unset — which works, right up until a restore:
# the secrets would then exist only inside the volume and could not be
# recovered independently of it. Rotating either invalidates all sessions and
# every in-flight CSRF token, which is disruptive rather than destructive.
# Generate each: openssl rand -hex 32
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
EXCALIDASH_JWT_SECRET=changeme_openssl_rand_hex_32
EXCALIDASH_CSRF_SECRET=changeme_openssl_rand_hex_32

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ExcaliDash OIDC client secret — LEAVE EMPTY until the Authentik side exists.
#
# 🚨 Unlike every other OIDC-off service in this fleet, ExcaliDash is UNUSABLE
# until this lands, and that is deliberate. Its only other mode, AUTH_MODE=local,
# gates registration behind a one-time admin setup code printed ONLY to the
# backend's stdout — a browser-plus-log-scrape wizard — and the documented way
# around that (DISABLE_ONBOARDING_GATE=true) leaves open registration on a
# service the whole tailnet can reach. Unusable-and-closed beats usable-and-open.
#
# EMPTY IS SAFE HERE, non-obviously: config.ts throws at startup (crash loop)
# when auth is enabled and any of OIDC_ISSUER_URL / OIDC_CLIENT_ID /
# OIDC_REDIRECT_URI is empty — but the CLIENT SECRET is NOT in that required
# set, because a public client is allowed. So the container boots with this
# blank and fails only at /auth/oidc/start.
#
# The Authentik application needs:
#   slug          excalidash
#   redirect URI  https://excalidash.svc.idanreed.com/api/auth/oidc/callback
#   a group named `excalidash-admins` (OIDC_ADMIN_GROUPS), or nobody is admin
#   an `email_verified=true` claim, or sign-in throws
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
EXCALIDASH_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
